Just thought of a few:

telekinesis
telekinetic control    ability to move (shoot) objects from a distance
			 maybe include zapping wands
object detection       so if you have tk and tkc, you can move/shoot
			 objects which you cant see
audio telepathy        as a form of magic mapping (use earplugs,
			 with the idea being a form of "radar")

Maybe these intrinsics would make the player too powerful;  
perhaps make tk/tkc incompatible with teleport/tpc (this
would give those particular rings a lot more power though).

Also definitely have monsters with these intrinsics; make it
not incompatible for them and make some obscure way for 
players to overcome the incompatibility ie polymorph and
eat all the rings.

I think cliffs onto other levels would be neat also, and
more dynamics to the structure of the level/dungeon ie
logs floating across rivers, magic forests, fires, floods,
locust swarms, elevator sections of floors which move up and
down levels, haunted houses, etc.  multiplayer could be 
implemented by making the penalty of killing a lower-level
player to be permanently achieving nontiming out extremely bad luck.
(leaves open the possibilty of cornering one and knocking
down hp to a level where the next grid bug will kill; demanding
all possessions in return for not doing this!)


